# This repo is meant to be cloned on Windows, Mac, and Linux alike, and the
# shell scripts here run under Git Bash on Windows and real bash elsewhere.
# A script committed from Windows with CRLF line endings still runs under
# Git Bash (it tolerates CRLF), but fails outright under any other bash
# (WSL, a container, a stricter CI runner). Force LF for every script this
# repo ships, regardless of which OS committed it.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=lf

# A commit made on Windows does not carry the executable bit at all (NTFS
# has no such bit for git to read), so a shell script committed there lands
# in the tree as mode 100644. `./install.sh` then fails with "Permission
# denied" on a clone that actually enforces the bit (Mac/Linux). There is no
# gitattributes setting that fixes this on its own: before committing a
# changed or new .sh file from a Windows checkout, run
#   git update-index --chmod=+x <path>
# (or set it once with `git add --chmod=+x` on first add) so the bit is
# recorded in the commit itself.
